{"header":{"numFound":19,"maxScore":16.812654,"queryTime":410,"page":1,"pageSize":10},"results":[{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Jiayi Wen","name":"Jiayi","surname":"Wen","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0003-4957-3531"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Dinghui Zou","name":"Dinghui","surname":"Zou","rank":2,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0301 basic medicine"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0303 health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"03 medical and health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"13. Climate action"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Sargassum"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seawater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"14. Life underwater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon Dioxide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Hydrogen-Ion Concentration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Photosynthesis"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Copper"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Interactive effects of increasing atmospheric CO2 and copper exposure on the growth and photosynthesis in the young sporophytes of Sargassum fusiforme (Phaeophyta)","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Little attention has been given to the combined effects of elevated atmospheric CO2-induced ocean acidification (OA) and heavy metal pollution on marine macroalgae at the young stage. This study investigated the mutual effects of copper (Cu) and elevated CO2 on the young sporophytes of brown macroalgae Sargassum fusiforme. A matrix of four copper concentrations, 0, 0.025, 0.075 and 0.15 mg‧L-1, and two levels of CO2 (ambient CO2: 400 μatm; elevated CO2: 1,000 μatm) were used. High concentration of copper exposure greatly depressed photosynthesis and growth of the young sporophytes of S. fusiforme by reducing the apparent photosynthetic efficiency (ɑ), maximum net photosynthetic oxygen evolution rate (Pmax), maximum photochemical quantum yield (Fv/Fm) and pigments content (Chl a and Car). While elevated CO2 alone had obscure impact on this alga. However, the inhibition of Cu stress on Fv/Fm was weakened by elevated CO2, which also decreased the light compensation point (Ic). Meanwhile, the Cu2+-induced ascent in the dark respiration rate (Rd) and superoxide dismutase (SOD) activity was mitigated under the growth with elevated CO2, suggesting an alleviated oxidative stress. Overall, we propose that, under CO2 enrichment condition, the young sporophytes of S. fusiforme may increase photosynthesis efficiency and synthesize less enzymatic antioxidants in face of increasing Cu stress."],"publicationDate":"2021-04-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Chemosphere","issnPrinted":"0045-6535","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"129397","vol":"269","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::f87f8d8218173b6298ef583ca51e2eee","originalIds":["S0045653520335955","10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397","50|doiboost____|f87f8d8218173b6298ef583ca51e2eee","33383248","3116116062"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"33383248"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":15.0,"influence":2.4246545E-9,"popularity":1.0983399E-8,"impulse":11.0,"citationClass":"C4","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"South China University of Technology","acronym":"SCUT","id":"openorgs____::f73a11bf6ae3971adf53c090f95fc071","pids":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"90610280"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q835366"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100005015"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"399382"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000417643838"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100005015"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q835366"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.79703.3a"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/0530pts50"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://en.scut.edu.cn/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"},{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397"}],"license":"Elsevier TDM","accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397"],"publicationDate":"2021-04-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::a386aefeb8857d7cb3b7dc6566e515b4","value":"Chemosphere"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"33383248"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33383248"],"publicationDate":"2021-02-24","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3116116062"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3116116062"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.chemosphere.2020.129397"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Noa Naiman","name":"Noa","surname":"Naiman","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Avner Gross","name":"Avner","surname":"Gross","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::11ce99853433ed31d00a1ddb311a339f","fullName":"Gilad Antler","name":"Gilad","surname":"Antler","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-6865-5412"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"The Effect of Ocean Acidification on Phosphorus Solubility from Wildfire Ash and its Role in Enhancing the Biological Carbon Pump","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Increasing atmospheric CO&amp;#8322; concentrations drives ocean acidification, potentially leading to substantial impacts on marine ecosystems and altering marine nutrient dynamics. Phosphorus (P) availability is a key limiting factor for primary productivity in the oceans. Atmospheric particles, such as wildfire ash, supply the oceans with substantial amounts of nutrients such as P. The solubility of P from aerosol particles, especially from wildfire ash, plays a critical role in oceanic nutrient cycles and may significantly impact the biological carbon pump, a key mechanism for atmospheric CO&amp;#8322; regulation.As ocean acidification continues and wildfires are projected to increase in intensity and severity with climate change, understanding how changes in seawater pH influence P release from wildfire ash is essential. This study aims to investigate the effect of past, present, and future seawater pH levels on P solubility from different wildfire ash under controlled laboratory conditions. Specifically, the study aims to examine how elevated CO&amp;#8322; levels, leading to lower pH (ocean acidification), impact the availability of P in wildfire ash compared to lower CO&amp;#8322; levels.Using artificial seawater and ash samples derived from Mediterranean and agricultural vegetation, this research will analyze P release patterns under a range of CO&amp;#8322; concentrations, encompassing current levels, future projections, and historical baselines.Preliminary results demonstrated a significant dependence of P release from wildfire ash on pCO&amp;#8322; concentrations and its influence on the pH. Elevated CO&amp;#8322; levels of the projected future and of ancient atmosphere enhanced P solubility in both Mediterranean vegetation and agricultural vegetation treatments while reduced levels of the preindustrial and pre-Holocene periods decreased P solubility. These findings are anticipated to shed light on the role of wildfire ash in marine nutrient dynamics and its broader impact on ocean productivity and the global carbon cycle, especially in regions experiencing increasing wildfire activity.These initial findings lay the groundwork for continued research, where I will investigate the cultivation of microalgae under controlled laboratory conditions at varying atmospheric CO2 concentrations. The research will focus on understanding how P release from wildfire ash, influenced by different CO2 levels, impacts the growth rate of phytoplankton. The experiments will assess the role of wildfire ash as a potential P source for phytoplankton grown in P-depleted water.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2025-03-18","publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":null,"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::6105df17cad990a56a9d7ece1d30c321","originalIds":["10.5194/egusphere-egu25-5059","50|doiboost____|6105df17cad990a56a9d7ece1d30c321"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5194/egusphere-egu25-5059"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":2.2497804E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Interuniversity Institute for Marine Sciences in Eilat","acronym":"IUI","id":"openorgs____::648bc203490fb90952905013e20422f2","pids":[{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q30293650"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q30293650"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/00pvs0d78"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.440849.5"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"000000040496208X"}],"countries":[{"code":"IL","label":"Israel"}],"websiteurl":"https://iui-eilat.huji.ac.il"},{"legalName":"Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","acronym":"BGU","id":"openorgs____::016a0e64dd9ec253b340b6c32724c327","pids":[{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100005005"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"351524"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100007621"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999846222"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000419370511"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q737332"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"124227911"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.7489.2"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q737332"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/05tkyf982"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100005005"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100007621"}],"countries":[{"code":"IL","label":"Israel"}],"websiteurl":"http://in.bgu.ac.il/en"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5194/egusphere-egu25-5059"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-egu25-5059"],"publicationDate":"2025-03-18","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::f6cf1daa013bb9c1315a66f7867bcd3b","fullName":"Jack, Schultz","name":"Jack","surname":"Schultz","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-7672-1547"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Dianna L, Berry Gobler","name":"Dianna L","surname":"Berry Gobler","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Craig S, Young","name":"Craig S","surname":"Young","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::7ea56de6dc4d94d779e2af5731d3ae4c","fullName":"Aleida, Perez","name":"Aleida","surname":"Perez","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-2508-0169"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Michael H, Doall","name":"Michael H","surname":"Doall","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Christopher J, Gobler","name":"Christopher J","surname":"Gobler","rank":6,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"hybrid","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Kelp"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Ocean Acidification"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Oceans and Seas"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seawater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Hydrogen-Ion Concentration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon Dioxide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Laminaria"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Edible Seaweeds"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Water Pollutants, Chemical"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Trace Elements"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Ocean acidification significantly alters the trace element content of the kelp, Saccharina latissima","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Seaweeds are ecosystem engineers that can serve as habitat, sequester carbon, buffer ecosystems against acidification, and, in an aquaculture setting, represent an important food source. One health issue regarding the consumption of seaweeds and specifically, kelp, is the accumulation of some trace elements of concern within tissues. As atmospheric CO2 concentrations rise, and global oceans acidify, the concentrations of elements in seawater and kelp may change. Here, we cultivated the sugar kelp, Saccharina latissima under ambient (~400 μatm) and elevated pCO2 (600-2400 μatm) conditions and examined the accumulation of trace elements using x-ray powder diffraction, sub-micron resolution x-ray imaging, and inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry. Exposure of S. latissima to higher concentrations of pCO2 and lower pH caused a significant increase (p < 0.05) in the iodine and arsenic content of kelp along with increased subcellular heterogeneity of these two elements as well as bromine. The iodine-to‑calcium and bromine-to‑calcium ratios of kelp also increased significantly under high CO2/low pH (p < 0.05). In contrast, high CO2/low pH significantly reduced levels of copper and cadmium in kelp tissue (p < 0.05) and there were significant inverse correlations between concentrations of pCO2 and concentrations of cadmium and copper in kelp (p < 0.05). Changes in copper and cadmium levels in kelp were counter to expected changes in their free ionic concentrations in seawater, suggesting that the influence of low pH on algal physiology was an important control on the elemental content of kelp. Collectively, these findings reveal the complex effects of ocean acidification on the elemental composition of seaweeds and indicate that the elemental content of seaweeds used as food must be carefully monitored as climate change accelerates this century."],"publicationDate":"2024-05-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","issnPrinted":"0025-326X","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"116289","vol":"202","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::7848d9103d2a55036628a0f1ae12bef6","originalIds":["S0025326X24002662","10.1016/j.marpolbul.2024.116289","50|doiboost____|7848d9103d2a55036628a0f1ae12bef6","38564822"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marpolbul.2024.116289"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"38564822"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":6.0,"influence":2.2757825E-9,"popularity":5.7782494E-9,"impulse":6.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Vanderbilt University","acronym":"Vanderbilt University","id":"openorgs____::e18a06920e42214398b85791c4efac6b","pids":[{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100007207"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q29052"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100006537"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100007206"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100007139"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100006010"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"37624759"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q29052"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100010901"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.152326.1"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000122647217"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"282250"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100007206"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100006537"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100010901"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"3152259"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100007182"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100007207"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"200719446"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100007182"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100006538"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100007139"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/02vm5rt34"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100006010"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100006538"}],"countries":[{"code":"US","label":"United States"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.vanderbilt.edu/"},{"legalName":"Stony Brook University","acronym":"SBU","id":"openorgs____::e672eb998b3c59e654af38cc44d0757b","pids":[{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100006802"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q969850"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q969850"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100007259"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000122169681"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100007259"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"59553526"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100009115"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100009115"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100006802"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.36425.36"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/05qghxh33"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"251208"}],"countries":[{"code":"US","label":"United States"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.stonybrook.edu/"},{"legalName":"Brookhaven National Laboratory","acronym":"BNL","id":"openorgs____::b1ce890327cd3deae1d99ef61de686b1","pids":[{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.202665.5"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:SCR_011123"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100006231"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100006231"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q5059647"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"53299"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:GAZ:00159027"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q5059647"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q585777"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000121884229"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q585777"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/02ex6cf31"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"200870766"}],"countries":[{"code":"US","label":"United States"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.bnl.gov/world/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marpolbul.2024.116289"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"hybrid"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpolbul.2024.116289"],"publicationDate":"2024-05-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::8fc00c1250704404f78f7e6bfb7555be","value":"Marine Pollution Bulletin"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"38564822"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marpolbul.2024.116289"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38564822"],"publicationDate":"2024-05-07","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::cfbc8c91c61cec57db81aed5cf685ca9","fullName":"Ana Paula, Ferreira","name":"Ana Paula","surname":"Ferreira","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6035-4546"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::a9431265cfabd99de093f1b1d9523cc4","fullName":"Glauco Barreto, de Oliveira Machado","name":"Glauco Barreto","surname":"de Oliveira Machado","rank":2,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-0147-1256"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Juan Carlos Farias, Pardo","name":"Juan Carlos Farias","surname":"Pardo","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Alessandra, Augusto","name":"Alessandra","surname":"Augusto","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Tânia Marcia, Costa","name":"Tânia Marcia","surname":"Costa","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Fosca Pedini Pereira, Leite","name":"Fosca Pedini Pereira","surname":"Leite","rank":6,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Oceans and Seas"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Climate Change"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Temperature"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Feeding Behavior"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon Dioxide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Hydrogen-Ion Concentration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Global Warming"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Sympatry"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Oxygen Consumption"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Ammonia"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Animals"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Amphipoda"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seawater"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"The effects of ocean warming and elevated CO2 on the feeding behavior and physiology of two sympatric mesograzers","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Atmospheric CO2 concentrations have increased significantly since pre-industrial times, leading to ocean warming and acidification. These environmental changes affect the physiology of marine organisms as they modify metabolic processes. Despite the critical role of temperature and pH in marine biology, studies of their combined effects are limited. This study investigated the interactive effects of ocean warming and acidification on the feeding behavior and physiology of two sympatric amphipods, Hyale niger and Cymadusa filosa. Using an orthogonal experimental design with two temperatures (27 °C and 30 °C) and two pH levels (7.8 and 7.5), we assessed feeding rates, respiration rates, ammonia excretion, and O/N ratios. Results indicated that C. filosa was less tolerant to these stressors than H. niger. While H. niger showed no significant changes between treatments, C. filosa showed reduced feeding rates and altered physiological responses to elevated temperature and decreased pH. Reducing the feeding rate of C. filosa may favor macroalgal biomass and strengthen bottom-up control in phytal communities. In addition, increased ammonia excretion in C. filosa suggests increased protein catabolism to meet energy demands at higher temperatures, despite reduced oxygen consumption. This indicates a compromised metabolism and a reduction in circulating oxygen capacity for C. filosa. The study shows heterogeneous responses to climate change, highlighting the need to assess combined environmental stressors in different species to accurately understand the impacts of climate change."],"publicationDate":"2025-06-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Comparative Biochemistry and Physiology Part A: Molecular &amp; Integrative Physiology","issnPrinted":"1095-6433","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"111831","vol":"304","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::1e002651008770e930dffe43945bb4f0","originalIds":["S1095643325000297","10.1016/j.cbpa.2025.111831","50|doiboost____|1e002651008770e930dffe43945bb4f0","40021047"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.cbpa.2025.111831"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"40021047"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":2.0,"influence":2.2031736E-9,"popularity":3.5200343E-9,"impulse":2.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"University of Agder","acronym":"UiA","id":"openorgs____::a7502dd2669be577007c95445ca412fa","pids":[{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.23048.3d"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"972805"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000404176230"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"200650556"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1470769"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1470769"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100012704"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/03x297z98"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"998822969"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.23048.3d"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100012704"}],"countries":[{"code":"NO","label":"Norway"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.uia.no/en"},{"legalName":"Sao Paulo State University","acronym":"UNESP","id":"openorgs____::3a8cba99f7929f01aa4435416d3af527","pids":[{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q10387795"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1817137"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"879563668"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q10387788"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q10387791"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q10387788"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q10302852"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q10387795"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/00987cb86"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q39487333"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1817137"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q39487333"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q10387791"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q18467813"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100009568"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q10387793"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q10302852"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.410543.7"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q10387797"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q10387793"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"000000012188478X"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"2938232"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q18467813"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q10387797"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100009568"}],"countries":[{"code":"BR","label":"Brazil"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.unesp.br/portal#!/eng"},{"legalName":"Norwegian Institute for Water Research","acronym":"NIVA","id":"openorgs____::6a5a391d24ee8b944cf6257d908e910d","pids":[{"scheme":"PIC","value":"997826585"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q21015880"},{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"NO1010"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100012111"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q21015880"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/03hrf8236"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000404479960"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100012111"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.6407.5"}],"countries":[{"code":"NO","label":"Norway"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.niva.no/en/om-niva/om-instituttet"},{"legalName":"State University of Campinas","acronym":"UNICAMP","id":"openorgs____::a635d7e44f7665917fa8259a8d0e45df","pids":[{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100006416"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q2060678"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000107232494"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100006417"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q2060678"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100006416"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.411087.b"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"181391015"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100006417"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999550857"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/04wffgt70"}],"countries":[{"code":"BR","label":"Brazil"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.unicamp.br/unicamp/?language=en"}],"communities":[{"code":"uarctic","label":"UArctic","provenance":null},{"code":"forthem","label":"FORTHEM Alliance","provenance":null},{"code":"enermaps","label":"Energy Research","provenance":null}],"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.cbpa.2025.111831"}],"license":"Elsevier TDM","accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cbpa.2025.111831"],"publicationDate":"2025-06-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::0644d92c0b09dcb4cff4697abe644c68","value":"Comparative Biochemistry and Physiology Part A Molecular & Integrative Physiology"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"40021047"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.cbpa.2025.111831"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40021047"],"publicationDate":"2025-04-11","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Yingya Chen","name":"Yingya","surname":"Chen","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Zhen Zhang","name":"Zhen","surname":"Zhang","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Jie Ma","name":"Jie","surname":"Ma","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::97d4f235e2af75d0c367a914f5a71bb2","fullName":"Ke Pan","name":"Ke","surname":"Pan","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-2931-1692"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Diatoms"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Ocean Acidification"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seawater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Hydrogen-Ion Concentration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon Dioxide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Copper"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Water Pollutants, Chemical"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Cellular and genetic responses of Phaeodactylum tricornutum to seawater acidification and copper exposure","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["The ongoing decline in seawater pH, driven by the absorption of excess atmospheric CO2, represents a major environmental issue. This reduction in pH can interact with metal pollution, resulting in complex effects on marine phytoplankton. In this study, we examined the combined impacts of seawater acidification and copper (Cu) exposure on the marine diatom Phaeodactylum tricornutum. Our data indicate that elevated pCO2 had a minor effect on the growth and photochemistry and overall performance of P. tricornutum. However, seawater acidification significantly influenced cell size, surface roughness, and adhesion. Higher pCO2 levels led to increased Cu accumulation in P. tricornutum under low ambient Cu concentrations, while significantly reducing Cu accumulation. The smaller cell size and reduced negative charge on the cell surface may explain the decreased Cu accumulation and toxicity. In response to metal stress, P. tricornutum upregulated Cu efflux to mitigate the increased Cu stress in acidified seawater. The expression of the metal transporter gene CTR1 and the reductase gene FRE1 were significantly downregulated, while ATPase5-1B was upregulated in cells exposed to elevated Cu concentrations at 1200 μatm pCO2. Our study provides useful insights into the interactions between metals and diatoms in an increasingly acidified ocean."],"publicationDate":"2025-02-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Marine Environmental Research","issnPrinted":"0141-1136","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"106928","vol":"204","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::b3823bafc8781b3a0777eff00e49dbac","originalIds":["S0141113624005890","10.1016/j.marenvres.2024.106928","50|doiboost____|b3823bafc8781b3a0777eff00e49dbac","39729905"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marenvres.2024.106928"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"39729905"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":2.2497804E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Hong Kong Polytechnic University","acronym":"HKPU","id":"openorgs____::5f8471cfd1554660ddb736792f1ab7f8","pids":[{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"23757778"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"268987"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"268078"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1333303"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100006066"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100004377"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100011650"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100011650"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1187271"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/00q4vv597"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.24515.37"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100022174"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999463169"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100006066"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.16890.36"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q99229082"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100004377"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100014819"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/0030zas98"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000417646123"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"997262918"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100022174"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000484971137"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"200769079"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/050h0vm43"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000419371450"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100014819"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"886266012"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1187271"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"14243506"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1333303"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100005950"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100005950"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.polyu.edu.hk/web/en/home/index.html"},{"legalName":"Shenzhen University","acronym":"SZU","id":"openorgs____::03b0b55dced73b74d394734165f3d4e5","pids":[{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100009019"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"3804886"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/01vy4gh70"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000104729649"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1945756"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.263488.3"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"180726961"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1945756"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100009019"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.szu.edu.cn/2014/en/"},{"legalName":"Guilin University of Technology","acronym":"GUT","id":"openorgs____::826ca93125b8f2e8368c500137864c14","pids":[{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"20259782"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100003457"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.440725.0"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000090500527"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"38706770"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q5615997"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q5615997"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100003457"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/03z391397"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://en.glut.edu.cn/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marenvres.2024.106928"}],"license":"Elsevier TDM","accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marenvres.2024.106928"],"publicationDate":"2025-02-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::1c783504bbddf15cfe2311114c3f1db1","value":"Marine Environmental Research"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"39729905"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marenvres.2024.106928"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39729905"],"publicationDate":"2025-04-29","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Chao, Long","name":"Chao","surname":"Long","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Yating, Zhang","name":"Yating","surname":"Zhang","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Zhangliang, Wei","name":"Zhangliang","surname":"Wei","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Lijuan, Long","name":"Lijuan","surname":"Long","rank":4,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Ocean Acidification"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Rhodophyta"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seawater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Nutrients"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Hydrogen-Ion Concentration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon Dioxide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Photosynthesis"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seaweed"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Edible Seaweeds"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"High nutrient availability modulates photosynthetic performance and biochemical components of the economically important marine macroalga Kappaphycus alvarezii (Rhodophyta) in response to ocean acidification","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Increased atmospheric CO2 concentrations not only change the components of inorganic carbon system in seawater, resulting in ocean acidification, but also lead to decreased seawater pH, resulting in ocean acidification. Consequently, increased inorganic carbon concentrations in seawater provide a sufficient carbon source for macroalgal photosynthesis and growth. Increased domestic sewage and industrial wastewater discharge into coastal areas has led to nutrient accumulation in coastal seawaters. Combined with elevated pCO2 (1200 ppmv), increased nutrient availability always stimulates the growth of non-calcifying macroalgae, such as red economical macroalga Gracilariopsis lemaneiformis. Here, we evaluated the interactive effects of nutrients with elevated pCO2 on the economically important marine macroalga Kappaphycus alvarezii (Rhodophyta) in a factorial 21-day coupling experiment. The effects of increased nutrient availability on photosynthesis and photosynthetic pigments of K. alvarezii were greater than those of pCO2 concentration. The highest Fv/Fm values (0.660 ± 0.019 and 0.666 ± 0.030, respectively) were obtained at 2 μmol L-1 of NO3-N at two pCO2 levels. Under the elevated pCO2 condition, the Chl-a content was lowest (0.007 ± 0.004 mg g-1) at 2 μmol L-1 of NO3-N and highest (0.024 ± 0.002 mg g-1) at 50 μmol L-1 of NO3-N. The phycocyanin content was highest (0.052 ± 0.012 mg g-1) at 150 μmol L-1 of NO3-N under elevated pCO2 condition. The malondialdehyde content declined from 32.025 ± 4.558 nmol g-1 to 26.660 ± 3.124 nmol g-1 with the increased nutrients at under low pCO2. To modulate suitable adjustments, soluble biochemical components such as soluble carbohydrate, soluble protein, free amino acids, and proline were abundantly secreted and were likely to protect the integrity of cellular structures under elevated nutrient availability. Our findings can serve as a reference for cultivation and bioremediation methods under future environmental conditions."],"publicationDate":"2024-02-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Marine Environmental Research","issnPrinted":"0141-1136","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"106339","vol":"194","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::1629eb716406cf2a6d59e6810603b8ee","originalIds":["S0141113623004671","10.1016/j.marenvres.2023.106339","50|doiboost____|1629eb716406cf2a6d59e6810603b8ee","38182500"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marenvres.2023.106339"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"38182500"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":10.0,"influence":2.4368256E-9,"popularity":8.4113E-9,"impulse":10.0,"citationClass":"C4","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","acronym":"UCAS","id":"openorgs____::bd84daa73666b8ede0e886f71fde9dac","pids":[{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"6704292"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q6544465"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000417978419"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.410726.6"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/05qbk4x57"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100015361"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100011332"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100011332"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q6544465"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100015361"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.ucas.ac.cn/"},{"legalName":"South China Sea Institute Of Oceanology","acronym":"SCSIO","id":"openorgs____::c74fe86b4cb3646732179ba692458da2","pids":[{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/0192yj155"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000417989724"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q30259667"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q30259667"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100010213"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.458498.c"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100010213"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://english.scsio.cas.cn/"},{"legalName":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","acronym":"CAS","id":"openorgs____::5529875fee5e1f070225a154ae69437b","pids":[{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100003165"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/034t30j35"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100012430"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"377856"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100003165"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q530471"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100013494"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100002367"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100018527"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100005151"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:SCR_012797"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000119573309"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100005151"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"19820366"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.9227.e"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q530471"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100018527"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100002367"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100012430"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100013494"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://english.cas.cn/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marenvres.2023.106339"}],"license":"Elsevier TDM","accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marenvres.2023.106339"],"publicationDate":"2024-02-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::1c783504bbddf15cfe2311114c3f1db1","value":"Marine Environmental Research"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"38182500"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.marenvres.2023.106339"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38182500"],"publicationDate":"2024-01-22","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::5567ccf8b4cf9e5d9cb835700b5b0eb8","fullName":"Aline Mega","name":"Aline","surname":"Mega","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-9386-2261"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Eva Calvo","name":"Eva","surname":"Calvo","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::fb456feac50796b7c9aa06c5131a1c66","fullName":"Leopoldo D. Pena","name":"Leopoldo","surname":"D. Pena","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6414-6293"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::874ff50dfa8f4063f7bc37b7308000b6","fullName":"Emília Salgueiro","name":"Emília","surname":"Salgueiro","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-1000-2977"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Andreia Rebotim","name":"Andreia","surname":"Rebotim","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::2df42da0d2c6a6f37a68bf02496abddc","fullName":"Antje Voelker","name":"Antje","surname":"Voelker","rank":6,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6465-6023"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Joana Cruz","name":"Joana","surname":"Cruz","rank":7,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::4c50758d3096ad24f78d020a17bb95c8","fullName":"Fátima Abrantes","name":"Fátima","surname":"Abrantes","rank":8,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-9110-0212"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"13. Climate action"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"14. Life underwater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"15. Life on land"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0105 earth and related environmental sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"&amp;#160;pH variations during the last and current interglacial stages at the western Iberian margin","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>The intricate interplay among atmospheric CO2 concentrations, surface ocean pH dynamics, and their profound impact on marine ecosystems is of paramount importance in the context of contemporary climate change. Pre-industrial atmospheric CO2 concentrations oscillated in phase with glacial-interglacial cycles, showcasing low levels during glacial periods and elevated concentrations during interglacial periods. Nevertheless, this natural variability has been significantly disrupted due to the surge in anthropogenic CO2 emissions over recent decades. According to the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change, if global atmospheric CO2 concentrations persist in rising at the current rate, it is anticipated that the average ocean pH will decrease by 0.3 pH units in surface waters by the conclusion of this century. This scenario could exacerbate the impacts already observed in marine calcifying organisms, including in marine calcifying organisms such as planktonic foraminifera, affecting their diversity, abundance, and calcification. The main objective of this study is to understand the surface ocean pH evolution in a seasonal upwelling region, during two distinct interglacial periods in Earth's history: the Marine Isotopic Stage 5e (MIS 5e), the last interglacial without anthropogenic influence; and the Holocene, the present interglacial but subjected to anthropogenic influence. In upwelling regions, the upwelling of aged and CO2-rich subsurface waters together with high rates of primary production and respiration, is expected to regionally amplify ocean acidification. This study concentrates on the reconstruction of surface ocean pH using boron isotopes in a surface planktonic foraminifera species, Globogerinoides bulloides. This species is typically found in upwelling regions and was preserved in the marine sediment corer MD03-2699 (39&amp;#176;02.20&amp;#8242;N, 10&amp;#176;39.63&amp;#8242;W). Our preliminary findings indicate a pH difference between MIS 5e and the Holocene, with lower pH values during the Holocene.&amp;#160; It is argued that during the Holocene, a potential increase in wind intensity may have triggered a strong and persistent upwelling increasing productivity and respiration, consequently leading to lower pH. Additionally, the increase of atmospheric CO2, reconstructed from Antarctic ice cores during this period could also contribute to the ocean pH reduction. These variations in upwelling and/or atmospheric CO2 could be a pivotal factor influencing the observed pH differences, contributing to our comprehension of natural pH variations on the western Iberian margin through advanced pH reconstruction techniques and other multi-proxy environmental data integration for both periods in the region.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2025-01-20","publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":null,"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::154ebe16bd9f916c7be732002e57aadc","originalIds":["10.5194/egusphere-egu24-722","50|doiboost____|154ebe16bd9f916c7be732002e57aadc"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5194/egusphere-egu24-722"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":2.2497804E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"University of Barcelona","acronym":"UB","id":"openorgs____::6c3442fa797102c1c5c1a4319fce4119","pids":[{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100005774"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q219615"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.5841.8"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000419370247"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/021018s57"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100006203"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"61406"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"71999127"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q219615"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:SCR_002575"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100006203"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999986387"},{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"ES0017"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100005774"}],"countries":[{"code":"ES","label":"Spain"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.ub.edu/web/ub/en/"},{"legalName":"Spanish National Research Council","acronym":"CSIC","id":"openorgs____::7b08393d24bb163bc4b5008322df6894","pids":[{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1024362"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:nlx_156803"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"5195182"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"134820265"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100003339"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1024362"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000121834846"},{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"ES1031"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100003339"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/02gfc7t72"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999991722"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:SCR_011534"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.4711.3"}],"countries":[{"code":"ES","label":"Spain"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.csic.es/"},{"legalName":"CENTRO DE CIENCIAS DO MAR DO ALGARVE","acronym":"CCMAR","id":"openorgs____::3053c65910d1c064799cb9a93e57e5cd","pids":[{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q64346559"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"998611994"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100019181"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/00me37y22"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q64346559"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100019181"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000403670042"}],"countries":[{"code":"PT","label":"Portugal"}],"websiteurl":"http://ccmar.ualg.pt"},{"legalName":"University of Algarve","acronym":"UAlg","id":"openorgs____::6d0736d581ce680f41d642d66af056cf","pids":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"71503853"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"000000009693350X"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.7157.4"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999863003"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/014g34x36"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1972136"},{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"PT0002"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"1919382"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1972136"}],"countries":[{"code":"PT","label":"Portugal"}],"websiteurl":"https://www.ualg.pt/home/en"},{"legalName":"Institute of Marine Sciences","acronym":"ICM","id":"openorgs____::a1e21078949ae0b12d64ad4129eb0520","pids":[{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"000000041793765X"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q11926742"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/05ect0289"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.418218.6"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q11926742"}],"countries":[{"code":"ES","label":"Spain"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.icm.csic.es/en"}],"communities":[{"code":"mes","label":"European Marine Science","provenance":null}],"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5194/egusphere-egu24-722"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-egu24-722"],"publicationDate":"2025-01-20","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Alcaraz-Rocha, Paulo","name":"Paulo","surname":"Alcaraz-Rocha","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Puig-Fábregas, Júlia","name":"Júlia","surname":"Puig-Fábregas","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Fuentes-Lema, A.","name":"A.","surname":"Fuentes-Lema","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Garrido, J. L.","name":"J. L.","surname":"Garrido","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Sobrino, Cristina","name":"Cristina","surname":"Sobrino","rank":5,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":[{"code":"ES","label":"Spain","provenance":null}],"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Effects of the atmospheric CO2 increase in pigment concentration in the Cyanobacteria synechococcus spp. from two differeent marine habitats","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Previous studies have shown that high CO2 levels expected for future scenarios of global change might result in phytoplankton with higher sensitivity to photoinhibitory conditions than those exposed to present CO2 levels. This response, mainly observed in diatoms, has been attributed to a decrease in the repair rates caused by the lower levels of enzymatic activity and cellular pools observed, but could also be attributed to greater damage related to decreased protection. In this study, we will focus on the effects of elevated CO2 on the components of the xanthophyll cycle, a pigment cycle involved in the dissipation of excessive energy in the cell. The CO2 effect will be tested on a globally distributed cyanobacteria species, Synechococcus spp., isolated from two different marine habitats: the strain WH7803, typical from coastal areas, is observed during transition periods between mixing and stratification, while the strain WH8102 is adapted to oligotrophic environments and appears in open-ocean waters. The cultures were acclimated during at least 3 weeks with current concentrations of atmospheric CO2 (400 ppmv CO2 = Low CO2) and with concentrations expected for future scenarios of climate change (1000 ppmv CO2 = High CO2). HPLC results showed that in Synechococcus spp. violaxanthin was first de-epoxidated to antheraxanthin and then to zeaxanthin, which relates to cell protection. Chlorophyll a and β-carotene concentrations were lower than zeaxanthin concentration in both strains. However, zeaxanthin concentration increased significantly under high CO2 conditions in the coastal strain after a perturbation but did not change in the open-ocean strain under similar conditions. The results from the coastal strain were more similar to those observed in coastal diatoms, which might imply that differences in functional traits between phytoplankton assemblages from open-ocean vs. coastal waters are more significant than their taxonomic features regarding responses to ocean acidification","This work was funded by the Ministery of Economy and Competitiveness under the project: Down-regulation of phytoplankon metabolism in a high CO2 world: Consequences for resistance to abiotic and biotic stress (CTM2014-59345-R)","Poster.-- VI International Symposium on Marine Sciences, Vigo (Spain), 20-22th June 2018","Peer reviewed"],"publicationDate":"2026-06-16","publisher":null,"embargoEndDate":null,"sources":null,"formats":null,"contributors":["Ministerio de Economía y Competitividad (España)"],"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"od______1106::53cca9e3118cfc92abdbaadcb8f06988","originalIds":["50|od______1106::53cca9e3118cfc92abdbaadcb8f06988","oai:digital.csic.es:10261/435869"],"pids":[{"scheme":"handle","value":"10261/435869"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":2.6085654E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Spanish National Research Council","acronym":"CSIC","id":"openorgs____::7b08393d24bb163bc4b5008322df6894","pids":[{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1024362"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:nlx_156803"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"5195182"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"134820265"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100003339"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1024362"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000121834846"},{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"ES1031"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100003339"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/02gfc7t72"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999991722"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:SCR_011534"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.4711.3"}],"countries":[{"code":"ES","label":"Spain"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.csic.es/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"opendoar____::c9f95a0a5af052bffce5c89917335f67","value":"DIGITAL.CSIC"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"handle","value":"10261/435869"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Conference object","urls":["http://hdl.handle.net/10261/435869"],"publicationDate":"2026-06-16","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::c9f95a0a5af052bffce5c89917335f67","value":"DIGITAL.CSIC"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::c9f95a0a5af052bffce5c89917335f67","value":"DIGITAL.CSIC"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Pamela A, Fernández","name":"Pamela A","surname":"Fernández","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Charles D, Amsler","name":"Charles D","surname":"Amsler","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Catriona L, Hurd","name":"Catriona L","surname":"Hurd","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Patricio A, Díaz","name":"Patricio A","surname":"Díaz","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::b7a6dd4b59828befe75abbfabdd58107","fullName":"Juan Diego, Gaitán-Espitia","name":"Juan Diego","surname":"Gaitán-Espitia","rank":5,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-8781-5736"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Erasmo C, Macaya","name":"Erasmo C","surname":"Macaya","rank":6,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::1b7fb6625e0f21ff3c66c2f08c03897a","fullName":"Andreas, Schmider-Martínez","name":"Andreas","surname":"Schmider-Martínez","rank":7,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0009-0009-2826-6971"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Ignacio, Garrido","name":"Ignacio","surname":"Garrido","rank":8,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::9e65dd89fe926a9dd36a9546d63efd2f","fullName":"Pedro, Murúa","name":"Pedro","surname":"Murúa","rank":9,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-1598-7261"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::3d67b092bc291f0e769347104c9d1c4d","fullName":"Alejandro H, Buschmann","name":"Alejandro H","surname":"Buschmann","rank":10,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-3246-681x"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Species Specificity"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Ocean Acidification"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Climate Change"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Oceans and Seas"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Antarctic Regions"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seawater"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Hydrogen-Ion Concentration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon Dioxide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Seaweed"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Carbon"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Ecosystem"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Diverse inorganic carbon uptake strategies in Antarctic seaweeds: Revealing species-specific responses and implications for Ocean Acidification","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Seaweeds are important components of coastal benthic ecosystems along the Western Antarctic Peninsula (WAP), providing refuge, food, and habitat for numerous associated species. Despite their crucial role, the WAP is among the regions most affected by global climate change, potentially impacting the ecology and physiology of seaweeds. Elevated atmospheric CO2 concentrations have led to increased dissolved inorganic carbon (Ci) with consequent declines in oceanic pH and alterations in seawater carbonate chemistry, known as Ocean Acidification (OA). Seaweeds possess diverse strategies for Ci uptake, including CO2 concentrating mechanisms (CCMs), which may distinctly respond to changes in Ci concentrations. Conversely, some seaweeds do not operate CCMs (non-CCM species) and rely solely on CO2. Nevertheless, our understanding of the status and functionality of Ci uptake strategies in Antarctic seaweeds remains limited. Here, we investigated the Ci uptake strategies of seaweeds along a depth gradient in the WAP. Carbon isotope signatures (δ13C) and pH drift assays were used as indicators of the presence or absence of CCMs. Our results reveal variability in CCM occurrence among algal phyla and depths ranging from 0 to 20 m. However, this response was species specific. Among red seaweeds, the majority relied solely on CO2 as an exogenous Ci source, with a high percentage of non-CCM species. Green seaweeds exhibited depth-dependent variations in CCM status, with the proportion of non-CCM species increasing at greater depths. Conversely, brown seaweeds exhibited a higher prevalence of CCM species, even in deep waters, indicating the use of CO2 and HCO3-. Our results are similar to those observed in temperate and tropical regions, indicating that the potential impacts of OA on Antarctic seaweeds will be species specific. Additionally, OA may potentially increase the abundance of non-CCM species relative to those with CCMs."],"publicationDate":"2024-10-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Science of The Total Environment","issnPrinted":"0048-9697","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"174006","vol":"945","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::41163f83cd1ad2e5aeb6e31284ac31e7","originalIds":["S0048969724041548","10.1016/j.scitotenv.2024.174006","50|doiboost____|41163f83cd1ad2e5aeb6e31284ac31e7","38889822"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2024.174006"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"38889822"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":5.0,"influence":2.2412934E-9,"popularity":5.148413E-9,"impulse":5.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Université Laval","acronym":"Université Laval","id":"openorgs____::400ebffa7ac0f5f7d7771257447f5508","pids":[{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/05qn5kv73"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:SCR_011335"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"352708"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1067935"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/04sjchr03"}